<section class="section"><h2>How to resolve a warning</h2><ol>
<li><strong>Shared hosting or DirectAdmin:</strong> send the report below to the hosting provider and request a patched PHP build for this domain. DirectAdmin is a control panel, not proof of a patch.</li>
<li><strong>Managed VPS:</strong> ask the administrator to update every affected web PHP runtime and restart workers. On an unmanaged VPS, have your server administrator apply the vendor packages.</li>
<li><strong>Recheck the website:</strong> load this file again after patching. Checking terminal PHP alone does not establish the website’s PHP version. Check each domain and have the provider confirm every worker.</li>
<li><strong>Keep applications maintained:</strong> patched PHP does not establish the security of WordPress, plugins, themes or custom code. A WAF or application update is not a replacement for a PHP runtime patch.</li></ol>
